Track 1: Cassiopeia Scrapes the Gantry
- Story & Context: In October 1968, Orlo Vane dragged a stolen brass refracting telescope and a pair of 100-watt amplifiers up five flights of iron stairs to the roof of Warehouse 14 during a strike that had paralyzed the docks. As the fog turned the harbor water into milk, an unflagged freighter sounded a 110-decibel horn blast that rattled the loose gravel under their boots, prompting the band to strike back with an open-throttle thrash skank beat while Vane split his reed screaming into the horn bell. The song captures that opening skirmish between human noise and maritime steel, marked by the snarled opening decree: "Align the finder-scope until the iron tastes like sulfur!"
