Track 2: Is That Aldebaran or the Port Bow?
- Story & Context: Written in the damp attic of dockworker and amateur astronomer Milo Chen, this track chronicles a terrifying acid trip where Chen sat shivering beneath a wet wool blanket, unable to tell whether the flickering red light in his telescope lens was a dying giant star or the prow of an oncoming supertanker drifting off-course into the jetty. The alto sax mirrors his manic confusion, trading hyper-speed thrash arpeggios with cavernous, distorted horn groans that sound like hull metal buckling against concrete pilings. Chen wept into the band's reel-to-reel microphone at three in the morning, murmuring the track’s haunted centerpiece: "Every star we named tonight is steering straight for our teeth."
