Track 3: Azimuth Bleed Through Wet Felt
- Story & Context: Legend says the tape master for this finale was ruined and saved in the same hour when a rogue sea spray soaked the band's portable recorder during a rooftop gale, coating the tape deck’s felt pressure pads with salt sludge. The resulting track plays back as a ghost-story dirge that accelerates without warning into a blinding 230-BPM thrash eruption, commemorating the night the harbor siren failed and three tugs navigated home solely by tracing the band’s saxophone squeals through the gloom. The final dying tape hiss carries Vane's raw, unamplified roar across the roof: "Sound your whistle three times long if you can see the sky burning."
